# SPEC — Onchain Identity

> Spec-first onchain identity protocol. Users register profiles on Base, resolve via ENS subdomains. Fully onchain, fully yours.

---

## Product

A permissionless identity protocol. Users create profiles with name, avatar, bio, and links. Profiles are registered as ENS subdomains under `base.eth`. Resolving `alice.base.eth` returns Alice's profile address.

### Flow: User creates a profile

```
User calls register("alice") → Registrar mints alice.base.eth → Profile contract stores avatar/bio/links → ENS Resolver maps name → address
```

### Flow: Someone looks up a profile

```
ENS resolution: alice.base.eth → Resolver → Profile address → read bio, avatar, links
```

## Architecture

| Contract | Role | Deploys to |
|----------|------|-----------|
| Profile | Stores user identity data (name, avatar, bio, links) | Base Sepolia |
| Registry | Maps ENS names to profile addresses | Base Sepolia |
| Resolver | ENS-compatible resolver returning profile metadata | Base Sepolia |
| Registrar | Registers subdomains under base.eth | Base Sepolia |
